+- Windows: `App::hardware_acceleration(false)` draws the app's window on the CPU only, with no GPU device, swap chain or GPU atlas copies. What only the GPU draws degrades instead of starting one (`cpu_boot::Scene::strict`): a blurred layer draws nothing, a turned layer draws unturned, a backdrop blur inside a layer, an effect slot and a native surface are left out, linear blending blends in sRGB. The window is opaque. A window also stays on the CPU, strict, when DXGI lists no hardware adapter (instead of WARP) and after the GPU failed its tries (frames that needed it used to stop). `ImageCache::file_fit_blurred` and `load_fit_blurred` decode a picture blurred on the image worker, so no sharp pixel of it is ever handed on.
